    "body": "Closes https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41697\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\nCurrently, when requesting workspace diagnostics, we have to wait for the whole request to finish. For larger projects this can take a long time.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nImplement partial results for workspace diagnostics.\r\n\r\nThere are other methods that also support partial results, but diagnostics is the only part of Neovim that I'm somewhat familiar/comfortable with, so I thought it would be a good place to start.\r\n\r\nI've added a partialResults field to client.lua that tracks inflight partial results and a function to handle them. In theory it could be used for other partial results, not just workspace diagnostics, well that's the idea at least.\r\n\r\nA few things to note:\r\n\r\nIt seems like some servers send partial result progress as positional params  the LSP I'm testing with does. I've copied the workaround from the vscode implementation, see [here](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-languageserver-node/blob/5010cdf9822e1038a30ee7eb6ee5d7aaa79acc4a/jsonrpc/src/common/connection.ts#L972).\r\n\r\nI'm not actually sure when we should be sending a partial result token to the server. I know that, for example, the `diagnosticProvider` capability does extend `WorkDoneProgressOptions`, but I don't know if `WorkDoneProgressOptions` is the same as partial results. I think it should be fine sending a token on every request. If the server doesn't support it, I assume it just won't report to `$/progress` and will just respond to the request with full results.\r\n",
